(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["ArraySymmetry", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"1fbbe818-a298-154a-867d-c3cf4bfd48e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArraySymmetry", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0f698ee3-684c-424f-b357-5212303be46f"],
 " ",
 "gives the declared index symmetry of arr."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"70bf485f-4929-014b-8275-edcb9c83cb3f"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"4ad71246-c210-7147-93d8-8b78e3dad9ff"],

Cell["\<\
The result is one of \"Rigid\", meaning no symmetry is claimed; \"Cyclic\", \
meaning the entries are invariant under cyclic permutation of the indices; or \
\"Symmetric\", meaning they are invariant under all permutations.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"330fb985-187d-d24a-8a70-5c6d259ccedd"],

Cell["\<\
Only a regular array can carry a symmetry other than \"Rigid\".\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9871eb37-1444-e844-a825-70ddc2f459f7"],

Cell["\<\
The symmetry is a declared property, not a computed one: ArraySymmetry \
reports what was declared. For a numerical array the declaration is verified \
against the entries when the array is built; for a symbolic array it is \
honoured by construction, equivalent index tuples naming the same entry.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fb9f6873-740d-4d43-ab65-7f9a92d0039d"],

Cell["\<\
A symmetric array is also cyclic, so the same entries may be declared either \
way. At order two the cyclic group is the symmetric group and the two \
coincide exactly.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7b1760f5-cdaa-9f48-9afc-b0505f4b2c1c"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry is the third criterion by which a Hypermatrix orders its arrays, \
taking \"Symmetric\" before \"Cyclic\" before \"Rigid\".\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3ccbdd69-5b6d-9349-ab11-12b9ed0f28b4"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"51af5b28-69b0-e144-ab92-23616b8ffd9a"],

Cell["\<\
ArraySymmetry @ NumericalArray[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, Automatic, #] & /@ \
{\"Rigid\", \"Cyclic\", \"Symmetric\"}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1689c8c9-9d09-e14e-a08a-1496db09b495"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Rigid\"\>", ",", "\<\"Cyclic\"\>", ",", "\<\"Symmetric\"\>"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"62ddd6b8-2861-e245-ba6a-54eae17eac30"],

Cell["\<\
The entries of the cyclic orbit of (1, 2, 3) are invariant under rotation but \
not under reflection, so they are cyclic and not symmetric:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"ea168097-f865-cd4f-a091-c169e1fe3424"],

Cell["\<\
cyc = Array[If[MemberQ[{{1, 2, 3}, {2, 3, 1}, {3, 1, 2}}, {##}], 1, 0] &, {3, \
3, 3}];
{ArraySymmetry @ NumericalArray[cyc, Automatic, \"Cyclic\"],
 Quiet @ NumericalArray[cyc, Automatic, \"Symmetric\"]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"41ce4688-429c-4c49-997c-e788fe46ff1d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Cyclic\"\>", ",", "$Failed"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->\
"17490ebd-dcc1-1541-a2e8-ce5bb8d3ce17"],

Cell["Source", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"a2149af0-49f3-c14c-b6a9-12b77d00740d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Defined in ",
 StyleBox["src/Hypermatrix.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Plain"],
 ", section ",
 "\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 "Array accessors",
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3d3d8380-f031-9a44-9202-df26ce8c950c"],

Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection",ExpressionUUID->"f7213bde-0dab-1e4b-9714-deac8bd8c1b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayOrder", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "17cc33d0-6581-984c-b959-3361570b3d08"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayDimensions", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cc617a99-da45-ea42-802a-2b69bc1e6d79"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["RegularArrayQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6f16c458-3614-744f-b069-96f3dcc89693"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["NumericalArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2b5389d6-6608-8145-af00-ca9f9cc30db3"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["SymbolicArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3833d0ae-1cbe-d449-91b8-782308e03b42"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypermatrix", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8616ced9-fba2-9e4a-92f7-da85946df43c"]
}], "SeeAlso",ExpressionUUID->"dc798be1-8c65-ca4c-9154-e38df334ed5a"]
},
